This disc contains video!Videos can be available in either "MPEG" or "Cinepak" format, or both. Both require Apple's Quicktime software. MPEG videos require the QuickTime MPEG Playback system extension as well. If you need to, you can install QuickTime and the MPEG extension from this disc, by clicking the "Install QuickTime" button in the UMP preferences dialog. MPEG video provides better audio and video quality than Cinepak, but requires a more powerful computer to play. Try MPEG first, and if playback quality is poor, try Cinepak (if it's available).To see a video, select it from the video icon (filmstrip) menu in Universal Media Player. It will start QuickTime's movie player application. Press the play button (right-pointing triangle) in the movie window to start play.Slower, older computers might have difficulty playing the video. Most PowerMacs should not have trouble.Enjoy!